# =============================================================================
# Dialog flows for the Unified Travel Agent's NeMo Guardrails layer.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE ACTUALLY DOES
# Colang flows here are deterministic, canonical-form-matched canned replies
# - not an LLM self-check, and not real request handling. NeMo's dialog
# rails embed the incoming message (FastEmbed), classify it against the
# "define user ..." examples below, and if it confidently matches, return
# the paired "define bot ..." line verbatim, skipping the LLM entirely.
# That only works for replies that don't need any real data - which is why
# only TWO flows exist below. Everything else a user can ask this app
# (search/book a flight or hotel, cancel a booking, look up past bookings,
# plan an itinerary, ask about a destination) requires an actual database
# lookup or tool call, which a static Colang bot line cannot do - it would
# return a fixed, ungrounded answer instead of the real result. Those
# requests are intentionally NOT modeled as Colang flows; they fall through
# untouched to the ADK agent pipeline described below.
#
# THE APP'S ACTUAL PROCESSES - WHICH AGENT DOES WHAT
# (Reference only - not executable Colang. Source of truth is
# adk_app/agents/root_agent.py; keep this in sync by hand if that changes.)
#
#   root_orchestrator (adk_app/agents/root_agent.py)
#     Never answers directly - reads the message and delegates to exactly
#     one of the four sub-agents below.
#
#     -> booking_agent (adk_app/agents/booking_agent.py)
#          Reacts to: searching, recommending, or booking a specific flight
#          or hotel; canceling a booking; "what have I booked" / "where have
#          I been" style questions about the user's own travel history; a
#          bare confirmation like "book it" once a search result is pending.
#          Tools: flights_tool, hotels_tool, booking_tool (confirm/cancel/
#          get_my_bookings) - the only agent that can read/write real
#          bookings or look up flight/hotel inventory.
#
#     -> itinerary_agent (adk_app/agents/itinerary_agent.py)
#          Reacts to: an explicit multi-day plan/itinerary request
#          ("plan my trip", "3 day itinerary"). Not a single hotel/flight
#          ask, even if it sounds like trip planning - that's booking_agent.
#          Tools: itinerary_tool.
#
#     -> destination_agent (adk_app/agents/destination_agent.py)
#          Reacts to: sights, food, culture questions about a place. No
#          hotel/flight capability.
#          Tools: destinations_tool.
#
#     -> travel_agent (adk_app/agents/travel_agent.py)
#          Reacts to: general travel inspiration/questions with no
#          reference to the user's own past activity and no specific
#          flight/hotel ask.
#
#   Every one of those requests still passes through this same guardrails
#   layer first (self_check_input below), and the agent's reply through
#   self_check_output, before reaching the user - Colang flows or not.
# =============================================================================

# --- Flow: greeting -----------------------------------------------------
# Real conversation history for this app shows a large share of sessions
# start with nothing but "Hello" - answering those with a fixed, on-brand
# line instead of a full LLM round trip through the orchestrator is both
# faster and more consistent than letting the model freestyle a greeting.
# Additive: only fires for a bare greeting with no other content. Anything
# else - "hello, book me a flight to Rome" - falls through to the ADK
# agents as normal.

define user express greeting
  "hi"
  "hello"
  "hey"
  "hello there"
  "hey there"
  "good morning"
  "good afternoon"
  "good evening"

define flow greeting
  user express greeting
  bot express greeting

define bot express greeting
  "Hello! I'm your Unified Travel Agent - I can help you search flights and hotels, plan an itinerary, or tell you about a destination. Where would you like to go?"

# --- Flow: capabilities --------------------------------------------------
# Same rationale as greeting, for "what can you do" / "help" style
# questions. The reply below must stay in sync with the agent map above -
# it's stating the same routing, just phrased for the user. Kept in sync by
# hand with _CAPABILITIES_PHRASES / CAPABILITIES_BOT_MESSAGE in
# guardrails/client.py - nothing enforces that automatically.

define user ask capabilities
  "what can you do"
  "help"
  "what can you help with"
  "what are your capabilities"
  "how can you help me"
  "what do you do"

define flow capabilities
  user ask capabilities
  bot express capabilities

define bot express capabilities
  "I'm your Unified Travel Agent. I can: search and book flights and hotels (and cancel or look up your past bookings), plan a multi-day itinerary, tell you about a destination's sights, food, and culture, or just talk through general travel ideas. What would you like to do?"
